    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.align\n\n### Description\n\nI'm using Lazy Nvim package manager with the following setup:\r\n```lua\r\n  {\r\n    \"echasnovski/mini.align\",\r\n    version = false,\r\n    mappings = {\r\n      start = \"ga\",\r\n      start_with_preview = \"gA\",\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n```\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nwrite two lines:\r\n```\r\na = 10\r\nxy = 20\r\n```\r\n\r\nselect them with ctrl-V and press `ga` and `=`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nShould be aligned by adding space before the first line's `=`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nSelecting text and then pressing ga (and delimiter) does not align the text.",
