            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Standalone repository works, same as 'mini.nvim' itself.\r\n\r\nYou don't have it working is because `require('mini.align').setup()` was not called. You can check it yourself by executing `:lua print(_G.MiniAlign)`: should print message starting with `table: ` and not `nil`.\r\n\r\nThe reason it doesn't work seems to be because 'lazy.nvim' can't yet autoload plugin if its main file is in Lua submodule (like 'lua/mini/align.lua', for example). It is a good idea to look at how LazyVim handles standalone 'mini.nvim' repositories. For example, [this](https://github.com/LazyVim/LazyVim/blob/main/lua/lazyvim/plugins/coding.lua#L86).\r\n\r\nTry using this config:\r\n```lua\r\n{\r\n  \"echasnovski/mini.align\",\r\n  version = false,\r\n  mappings = {\r\n    start = \"ga\",\r\n    start_with_preview = \"gA\",\r\n  },\r\n  config = function(_, opts)\r\n    require(\"mini.align\").setup(opts)\r\n  end,\r\n},\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2023-02-19T16:55:34Z",
