            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "You're absolutely right. I think though that it is not entirely clear to beginners how do to the call to `require('mini.align').setup()` and having\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  \"echasnovski/mini.align\",\r\n  version = false,\r\n  config = function(_, opts)\r\n    require(\"mini.align\").setup(opts)\r\n  end,\r\n}\r\n```\r\ninstead of \r\n```\r\n{ 'echasnovski/mini.align', version = false },\r\n```\r\nin the _Standalone_ section for lazy.nvim would ease the installation process. (P.S. thanks for your great work!)",
